  "strDescriptionEN": "Gwion Dafydd Rhys Edwards (born 1 March 1993) is a Welsh professional footballer who plays as a winger for Morecambe. He is a former Wales Under-21 international. \r\nAfter spells with clubs including Aberystwyth Town and Cardiff City, Edwards joined Swansea City Football Club as an U15. Rising up through the Swansea youth system, Edwards signed his first professional contract, a 3-year deal, with Swansea City after a successful 2010\u201311 season. He went on to help Swansea win the FAW Welsh Youth Cup and was a permanent fixture in Swansea Reserve team, winning Reserve Team Player of the Year in 2011\u201312. \r\nOn 24 June 2016, Edwards joined League One side Peterborough United on a three-year deal for an undisclosed fee.",
